{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.4,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["D9", "D10"],
      "pins": ["U16.6", "U16.7", "U9.6", "U9.7", "J16.5", "J16.7", "J22.5", "J22.7"],
      "nets": ["NET0033", "NET0183", "NET0170", "NET0184"],
      "observed": "On the CAN differential pairs (the lines running from the isolated CAN transceivers U16/U9 to the M12 CAN connectors J16 'CAN Interface A' and J22 'CAN Interface B') the only passive components shown are the 120R termination resistors R75/R29 behind SW5; no CDSOT23-SM712 (or any other TVS/ESD) diode array is drawn anywhere on the CAN0/CAN1 pair nets across the CAN BUS sheets.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table states that D9 and D10, CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays, are placed on CAN0_P/N and CAN1_P/N for CAN-bus transient/ESD protection, and that this matches the documented intended part family (twistedfields-notes.txt 'TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG').",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "D9, D10 — CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N, CAN1_P/N | CAN bus transient/ESD protection | docs/twistedfields-notes.txt lists \"TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG\" as the intended part family for this role; the netlist's CDSOT23-SM712 matches this documented choice."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "CAN BUS sheets: transceiver outputs to J16/J22 carry only R75 120R / R29 120R (SW5 termination); no SOT23 TVS array symbol appears on the CAN pair nets."}
      ],
      "impact": "The two external CAN buses lose the specified transient/ESD protection. Normal communication is unaffected, but the CAN transceivers and the long motor-controller cabling are no longer clamped against surges/ESD as intended, so a bus transient can damage the front-end or corrupt frames — a deviation from the documented protection scheme.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build matches the spec on every functional block I could verify (16 MHz CAN crystals, MCP2515 + isolated transceivers, SN74LVC1G07 e-stop sinks, LTC4412 + P-MOS ideal diode, ISL54222 muxes, WS2812B string, CM4 pin mapping cross-checked against the Hirose mirror), but the CDSOT23-SM712 TVS arrays the spec places on the CAN differential pairs are absent from the drawing, leaving CAN0/CAN1 without the documented transient/ESD protection."
}

